 "script": [
  "About two hundred thousand miles from Earth, an explosion tore through Apollo 13.",
  "It was April 1970, and three astronauts were on their way to the Moon.",
  "Then an oxygen tank burst, and the crew radioed: Houston, we've had a problem.",
  "Their spacecraft was bleeding oxygen and losing power.",
  "So they climbed into the lunar module, Aquarius, and used it as a lifeboat.",
  "It was built to keep two men alive for two days. Now it had to keep three alive for four.",
  "Then carbon dioxide began to build up. The spare filters were the wrong shape.",
  "Engineers in Houston improvised a fix from bags, cardboard and tape, and talked the crew through building it.",
  "To get home, Apollo 13 swung around the far side of the Moon.",
  "Four days after the explosion, the capsule splashed down in the Pacific.",
  "All three men came home. NASA called it a successful failure."
 ],
